<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Dries Q2 pre-capex net drops slightly.</title>
<headline>Dries Q2 pre-capex net drops slightly.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-07-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Quarter to end-June versus preceding quarter</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit before capital spending   177.56 vs 182.02</p>
<p>    Capital spending			   139.46 vs 132.13</p>
<p>Gold output (kg)</p>
<p>    - East Dries			    6,518.3   vs 6,354.2</p>
<p>    - West Dries			    5,956.4   vs 5,784.9</p>
<p>    - Reclamation plant		    192.9    vs 83,2</p>
<p>Tonnes milled/treated</p>
<p>    - East Dries				595,000 vs 640,000</p>
<p>    - West Dries				697,000 vs 694,000</p>
<p>    - Reclamation plant		     580,000 vs 430,000</p>
<p>Yield (gram/t)</p>
<p>    - East Dries				   11.0 vs 9.9</p>
<p>    - West Dries				    8.5 vs 8.3</p>
<p>    - Reclamation plant			   0.3 vs 0.2</p>
<p>Cost (rand/kg)</p>
<p>    - East Dries				 31,427 vs 31,752</p>
<p>    - West Dries				 38,645 vs 39,169</p>
<p>Revenue (rand/kg)</p>
<p>    - East Dries				 49,371 vs 51,954</p>
<p>    - West Dries				 49,289 vs 51,612</p>
<p>Full name: Driefontein Consolidated Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - The company said tonnage milled at East Dries is expected to increase in the next quarter with the current yield being maintained.</p>
<p>- It said current production levels at West Dries are expected to be maintained in the next quarter at the current yield.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
